---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_672",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 672,
  "text": "[[2903.1]] <b>511.  De legum interpretatione« Excerpta annotata ex corpore juris civilis [1677 (?)]</b>\n [[2903.3]] <tab/>[1677 (?)]\n[[2903.8]] <tit2><b>De legum interpretatione</b></tit2> </p>\n<p> [[2903.9]] Cum <Fn>Cum <i>bis</i> debet <i>durch Anführungszeichen am Rande hervorgehoben</i>.</Fn> in uno casu sententia (legum) manifesta est, is qui jurisdictioni praeest ad\n[[2903.10]] similia procedere atque ita jus dicere debet. (+ <i>Ad similia</i> inquam id est quae tendunt ad\n[[2903.11]] eandem utilitatem +) l. 12. et seq. <i>de Leg.</i> adde l. <i>de quibus</i> 32 eod. <i>quoties deficit actio\n[[2903.12]] vel exceptio, utilis actio vel exceptio danda est</i> l. <i>quoties</i> 21 <i>de praescript. verb.</i> </p>\n<p> [[2903.13]] Lex <Fn>Lex <i>bis</i> interpretatione <i>durch Anführungszeichen am Rande hervorgehoben</i>.</Fn> utilis reipublicae adjuvanda est interpretatione. l. <i>hoc modo</i> 64. <i>de condit. et\n[[2903.14]] dem</i>. </p>\n<p> [[2903.15]] Quod vero contra rationem juris receptum est non est producendum ad consequentias,\n[[2903.16]] l. <i>quod vero</i> 14 <i>de Leg.</i> add. l. <i>quod non</i> 39. eod. (+ cessante porro ratione legis lex\n[[2903.17]] ipsa cessat, itaque +) quod favore quorundam constitutum est, quibusdam casibus ad\n[[2903.18]] laesionem eorum nolumus inventum videri, l. <i>quod favore</i> 6. C. <i>de Leg.</i> (add. l. <i>nulla\n[[2903.19]] juris ratio</i> 25. D., eod. l. <i>plures</i> 18. in fin. C. <i>de fide instrum.</i> Exempla sunt in l. <i>carbonianum</i>\n[[2903.20]] 3 § <i>divus enim De Carbon. edict.</i> et l. <i>non eo minus</i> 14 C. <i>de procur.</i> et l. <i>cum\n[[2903.21]] hi</i> 8 § <i>eam transact.</i> D. <i>de transact.</i> et l. <i>contra</i> 28. in princ. <i>de pact.</i>). </p>\n<p> [[2903.22]] Etsi <Fn>Etsi <i>bis</i> subveniendum <i>durch Anführungszeichen am Rande hervorgehoben</i>.</Fn> nihil facile mutandum in solennibus tamen ubi evidens aequitas postulat subveniendum\n[[2903.23]] est, l. <i>etsi nihil. </i> [183.] <i>de Reg. jur.</i> l. <i>in omnibus</i> 90 <i>de Reg. jur.</i> Exempla sunt\n[[2904.1]] in l. <i>in summa</i> 2. § <i>quanquam</i> D. <i>de aqua pluv. arc.</i> l. <i>filio praeterito</i> 17. <i>de injust. test.</i>\n[[2904.2]] l. <i>ait praetor</i> 1. <i>de in int. restit.</i> </p>\n<p> [[2904.3]] Plane in re dubia melius est verbis edicti servire, l. 1. § <i>sed si sciente</i> <i>de exerc. act.</i>\n[[2904.4]] (et) non aliter a significatione verborum recedi oportet quam cum manifestum est aliud\n[[2904.5]] sensisse testatorem, adde l. <i>sicut</i> 8. § <i>si debitori</i> D. <i>Ubi pignus vel hypoth. solv.</i> l. <i>si vero</i>\n[[2904.6]] 64. § <i>de viro</i> in f. D. <i>solut. matrim.</i> (nam) contra legem facit qui id facit quod lex\n[[2904.7]] prohibet, in fraudem vero legis qui salvis verbis legis sententiam ejus circumvenit,\n[[2904.8]] l. <i>contra legem</i> 29. <i>de Leg.</i> (sed) non dubium est contra legem committere eum, qui verba\n[[2904.9]] legis amplexus contra legis nititur voluntatem, nec poenas legibus insertas evitabit qui se\n[[2904.10]] contra juris sententiam saeva (+ lego: <i>scaeva</i> +) praerogativa verborum fraudulenter\n[[2904.11]] excusat. </p>\n<p> [[2904.12]] Benignius leges interpretandae sunt, ut voluntas eorum conservetur, l. <i>benignius</i> 18.\n[[2904.13]] <i>de Leg.</i> adde l. <i>nulla</i> 25. <i>de Leg.</i> l. <i>semper</i> [56.] et l. <i>ea quae</i> in fin. <i>de R. I.</i> Exempla sunt\n[[2904.14]] in l. <i>non sine ratione</i> 5. § <i>quamvis</i> C. <i>de bonis quae liberis.</i> l. <i>per fundum</i> 11. D. <i>de servit.\n[[2904.15]] rustic. praed.</i> </p>\n<p> [[2904.16]] Beneficium <Fn>Beneficium <i>bis</i> interpretari <i>durch Anführungszeichen am Rande hervorgehoben</i>.</Fn> imperatoris ... debemus quam plenissime interpretari, l. <i>beneficium</i> 3.\n[[2904.17]] <i>de const. princ.</i> (exemplum est in l. 2. C. <i>de bonis vac.</i>) (+ in legibus interpretandis\n[[2904.18]] adhiberi potest argumentum quod vocant a contrario sensu, exempli causa +) cum lex in\n[[2904.19]] praeteritum quid indulget in futurum vetat, l. <i>cum lex</i> 22. <i>de Leg.</i>\n[[2905.1]] <tit2><b>De Legum potestate</b> </tit2> </p>\n<p> [[2905.2]] Leges <Fn>Leges <i>bis</i> referat <i>durch Anführungszeichen am Rande hervorgehoben</i>.</Fn> et constitutiones futuris certum est dare formam negotiis non ad facta praeterita\n[[2905.3]] revocari, nisi nominatim et de praeterito tempore et adhuc pendentibus negotiis\n[[2905.4]] cau[sa]tum sit. l. <i>leges</i> 7. C. <i>de Leg.</i> (+ sed et hoc casu si appellatum sit +) justum nobis\n[[2905.5]] visum est ut secundum eas leges praedicta appellationis causa examinaretur quae tempore\n[[2905.6]] prolatae valuerint sententiae ... tametsi legem postea promulgari contigerit quae novi\n[[2905.7]] aliquid disponat, et vigorem suum vel ad praeterita etiam negotia referat. Novell. 115.\n[[2905.8]] princip. </p>\n<p> [[2905.9]] (+ Hic dubia nascuntur, videtur enim rationis esse ut distinguatur inter leges quae jus\n[[2905.10]] vetus interpretantur, et quae novum condunt; illas aequum, has iniquum est praeteritis et\n[[2905.11]] pendentibus causis accomodari, imo poenae lege nova definitae factis ante legem irrogari\n[[2905.12]] non posse videntur; et si testamentis nova forma praescriberetur, pertineret ad testamenta\n[[2905.13]] post legem condita. Sed hoc discrimen non satis observare videtur Imperator; nam si\n[[2905.14]] nominatim cavetur de praeteritis causis lege comprehendendis, signum est legem esse\n[[2905.15]] interpretatricem tantum, quo posito vim suam dudum habuit, tametsi id non omnibus\n[[2905.16]] esset manifestum, ac proinde etiam ad causas pertinet, in quibus a sententia lata appellatum\n[[2905.17]] est. +) Princeps legibus solutus est, Augusta autem licet legibus soluta non est.\n[[2905.18]] Princeps tamen eadem illi privilegia tribuit, quae et ipse habet, l. <i>princeps</i> 31. <i>de Leg.</i> </p>\n",
  "number": "511.",
  "title": "De legum interpretatione« Excerpta annotata ex corpore juris civilis",
  "date": "[1677 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:511. De legum interpretatione« Excerpta annotata ex corpore juris civilis [1677 (?)] [1677 (?)] De legum interpretatione Cum Cum bis debet durch Anführungszeichen am Rande hervorgehoben. in uno casu sententia (legum) manifesta est, is qui jurisdictioni praeest ad similia procedere atque ita jus dice...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>